    "title": "Stop & Shop to close several hours early this day. What to know",
    "text": "Stop & Shop is closing most of its grocery stores several hours early this Sunday.Easter is Sunday, April 5, this year, and many supermarkets across the country are closing for part or all of the day to give employees the opportunity to spend time with loved ones.Stop & Shop, which operates more than 360 stores on the East Coast, will close many of its Rhode Island locations before dinnertime that day.Here's what to know about Stop & Shop's Easter hours.Many Stop & Shop stores are slated to close early on Sunday, April 5.Is Stop & Shop open on Easter 2026?Most Rhode Island Stop & Shop stores will be open until 5 p.m. on Easter Sunday, according to the supermarket's website.This includes the locations in Providence, Cranston, Warwick, Narragansett, and Newport.Those stores will be open regular hours on Good Friday (April 3) and the Saturday before Easter (April 4).More: Market Basket closed on Easter Sunday and not the only ones. See listOther stores, such as Price Rite and BJ's Wholesale Club, will also have limited hours on Easter Sunday. Some supermarkets, like Market Basket, ALDI, and Dave's Fresh Marketplace, will be closed entirely that day.This article originally appeared on Cape Cod Times: Stop & Shop will close early on Easter Sunday. Here's what we know",
